            "title": "Canada names gas plant, port, mines as major projects to be sped up",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "OTTAWA (Reuters) -Canada named five major projects on Thursday it said would be eligible for fast-track approvals as part of a campaign to diversify the economy and reduce reliance on the United States as tariffs bite.  The government of Mark Carney, frustrated by a complex process that means it can take companies a decade or more to obtain approval for a mine or a pipeline, has set up a major projects office designed to slash red tape.  Among the five projects is a plan to double production of liquefied natural gas at the Shell-led LNG Canada plant in the western province of British Columbia.",
